	"nodes":[
		{"id":"b89443064fdbf84d","x":-240,"y":-180,"width":580,"height":360,"type":"text","text":"## Open Telemetry\n\nOpen telemetry is a vendor agnostic observability framework\n\n* Helps with the generation, processing and transmission of different types of telemetry data.\n\t* Metrics\n\t* Traces\n\t* Logs\n* Open framework managed by the cloud native computing foundation, supported by multiple vendors."},
		{"id":"56a46f814818944b","x":-620,"y":-540,"width":440,"height":240,"type":"text","text":"## Instrumentation\n\nAllows generated of signals to observe the system, can be done with language specific libraries implemented by Open Telemetry"},
		{"id":"4d2c0488c8b4e6af","x":-130,"y":-540,"width":360,"height":240,"type":"text","text":"## OTLP\n\nData generated by service with open telemetry protocol which describes properties of the system being observed. Means data from different types of services can be correlated together and compared."},
		{"id":"34fe10ce17d2c928","x":280,"y":-540,"width":400,"height":240,"type":"text","text":"## Collector \n\n"}
